Z||000064||BBBAD GT||12-03-2000||11:10 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Will:<BR><B>TPI runners are made of thin wall aluminum tubing. There's no material there that can be extrude honed.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Let me give the Ford side, which is almost the same situation.  When the GT40 intake came out back in the late 80's, it was wonderful for 302's, because it was designed for just 302's.  When Ford made a lower manifold to fit 351's with the stock GT40 upper, guys with a built 351+ cu in had trouble with it breathing above 4500 rpms.  Why?  Because the upper runners were designed for only 302 cu in, and because its made of thin wall tubes, it wasn't an extrude hone canidate. It gave great torque down low, but no power up top.  Guys with built 351's were only putting out 300-320 rwhp, and with only a change of intakes with a free breathing one, would see a min of 50 rwhp pick up. <P>This is very similar to the TPI, which I believe was originally designed for 305's, and not 350's.  With my limited knowedge of Chevy's, I believe when guys start punching out their 350 TPI's to 383, it pretty much dies above 4k rpms, limited by the intake.  It sounds like Will has a handle on the TPI system, which has confirmed my suspension on the TPI's on larger cu in motors (unmodified of course).  <P>Just thinking out loud....<BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000065||bubbajoexx||12-05-2000||11:23 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Will:<BR><B>TPI runners are made of thin wall aluminum tubing. There's no material there that can be extrude honed.<P><BR>     How much would extrude honing affect the performance of the stock Fiero intake system/manifolds?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You do not have to use stok runners there are after market runners that flow amazing amounts of air soas to make big hp with a tpi||||reg||1
Z||000066||Will||12-06-2000||12:39 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by bubbajoexx:<BR><B> You do not have to use stok runners there are after market runners that flow amazing amounts of air soas to make big hp with a tpi</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Sounds like someone didn't read the REST of the thread...<P>Go up about 18 posts and read my post about siamesed runners.||||reg||1
